+/*
+ * /dev/konacon - a write-only console for userland.
+ *
+ * The kernel log already reaches the panel through cons_ops, but userland has
+ * no tty on this port: /dev/console resolves through cnopen -> cndev ->
+ * km_tty[0] -> kmopen, and that path does not complete here yet. Rather than
+ * fight the tty layer for a bring-up test, expose the framebuffer console as a
+ * plain character device: whatever a process writes is drawn directly.
+ */
+/*
+ * Minimal frame buffer console. The tty console does not complete on this board
+ * (cnopen -> cndev -> km_tty[0] -> kmopen), so userland output is drawn here
+ * instead: /dev/konacon feeds this one character at a time through the kernel's
+ * own frame buffer mapping. 5x12 glyphs from the firmware font, scale 2.
